{
  "style": "discriminated-union",
  "$comment": "Golden fixture for the §5.6 process `runtime` shape (Phase 9 / M5-0), stored in stac_higher.process_revisions.runtime. Consumed by app/src/__tests__/contract-fixtures.test.ts (processRuntimeSchema) and services/pipeline/tests/test_contract_fixtures.py (parse_process_runtime). THE SLICE-1 ASYMMETRY IS DELIBERATE AND PINNED HERE: the shape CARRIES the `container` arm so nothing is foreclosed, and the pipeline reader accepts it, while the app's write gate REJECTS it — user-supplied images are a supply-chain review surface that stays out of the first accreditation scope (spec §4). Every `container` case below is therefore app: reject / pipeline: accept. `memory_mb` and `timeout_seconds` become the executor's per-run HostConfig limits and wall-clock kill (ADR 0013); `retry` reuses the queue RetrySpec shape from §5.1's delivery config verbatim. `network` (GOES spec §4, ADR 0018) is the egress profile — `level` in isolated|inputs|hosts|open with `hosts` non-empty iff level is `hosts` — and carries a SECOND slice-1 asymmetry of the same kind: the reader accepts every level (so no revision changes meaning when the egress proxy lands) while the app's write gate accepts only `isolated` until then; malformed network blocks are reject/reject on both sides. `runtime_image` (X-queue spec §8) is an ALIAS of a platform-built image — `default` | `stactools` — that the pipeline resolves at launch through PROCESS_RUNTIME_IMAGE / PROCESS_RUNTIME_IMAGE_STACTOOLS; it is not `image` (a user-supplied reference, still refused). Absent ⇒ `default` on both sides, since every revision stored before X-3 lacks it; an alias outside the set is reject/reject — the pipeline reader refuses it and the run dies as an unusable revision, the app never stores it.",
  "discriminator": "kind",
  "variants": {
